# Commit Message Format
# feat: Complete Day/Week X - Brief description
#
# Examples:
# feat: Complete Day 7 - State management and configuration fixes
# feat: Complete Week 1 - Frontend development and comprehensive refactoring
# fix: Resolve build errors in production environment
# docs: Update API documentation for authentication
# chore: Update dependencies to latest versions
#
# Guidelines:
# - Use "feat:" for new features or major milestones (Day/Week completions)
# - Use "fix:" for bug fixes
# - Use "docs:" for documentation only changes
# - Use "chore:" for maintenance tasks
# - Use "refactor:" for code refactoring
# - Use "test:" for adding or updating tests
#
# Body (optional):
# - Explain WHAT changed and WHY (not HOW)
# - Reference issues/tickets if applicable
#
# Footer (auto-added by system):
# 🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)
#
# Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

